**Install**
Download the `.zip` file from GitHub:
```
https://github.com/timeroll/TimeLord
```
Extract it to your working directory.
```
cd TimeLord
```

**Build**
Open the command prompt/terminal and run these commands:
```bash
dotnet new console --verbosity=debug
dotnet sln TimeLord.sln
cd TimeLord
dotnet build
```

**Install**
If you want the installer to run automatically, add these lines:
```bash
dotnet publish -c Release -r win-x64
```

**Script**
The core loop tracks time and tracks browser/app usage. The key part is handling screenshots. Time Lord has a built-in function called `TimeLord.SaveScreenshot()` that writes to a local directory. You can extend it to write to a file instead of the clipboard.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Diagnostics;
using System.Text;
using System.IO;

public class TimeLordSavescreenShot
{
    private readonly TimeLordClient clients;
    public TimeLordSavescreenShot(TimeLordClient clients)
    {
        this.clients = clients;
    }

    public void StartUsingScreenShot()
    {
        var screen = Console.ReadLine(); // Give user input
        if (screen == "Use ScreenShot")
        {
            // Capture screenshot
            string path = Path.Combine(Environment.GetFolderPath(Environment.SpecialFolder.Desktop), "ScreenShot.png");
            if (File.Exists(path)) File.Delete(path);
            File.WriteAllBytes(path, clients.SaveScreenShot(screen));
        }
        else File.WriteAllBytes(Path.Combine(Environment.GetFolderPath(Environment.SpecialFolder.Desktop), "ScreenShot.png"), clients.SaveScreenShot(screen));
    }
}
